E. Backtest methodology (text for Claude)
- Define "event" as a signal at timestamp t with predicted prob p and target asset.
- Define outcome window W (e.g., 3 days). For each signal, compute whether return over W exceeded target T (e.g., +2% for long signals).
- For each threshold tau in [0.0,1.0], compute:
  - Signals with p >= tau
  - TP = signals where outcome was positive; FP otherwise
  - Precision = TP / (TP + FP); FPR relative to all non-events
- Build calibration bins (10 or 20 bins), for each bin compute empirical hit rate. Use isotonic regression or Platt scaling to map raw_score -> calibrated prob.
- Choose recommended_abstain_threshold to meet target FPR or target precision based on operator preference.

